const e='### How to Start AI Meeting Transcription with SeaMeet Note Taker\n\nYou can invite the SeaMeet Copilot to join the meeting in Google Calendar or Google Meet. Once the meeting starts, the Copilot will automatically join and begin transcription.\n\n### Which Meeting Platforms Does SeaMeet AI Meeting Assistant Support?\n\nCurrently, SeaMeet supports transcribing meetings held in Google Meet, Microsoft Teams, Discord and Phone Calls with Twilio and PBX. More meeting platforms will be supported in the future.\n\n### What Languages Does SeaMeet AI Transcription Support for Meeting Notes?\n\nSeaMeet currently supports transcribing meetings in the following languages: English (United States, Singapore), Spanish (Spain, Latin America), French, German, Polish, Danish, Traditional Chinese, Cantonese (Hong Kong, Traditional), Cantonese (Simplified), Japanese, Korean, Vietnamese, Thai and Hindi. More languages will be added in the future.\n\n### How to Collaborate with Team Members on Meeting Minutes Using SeaMeet\n\nAbsolutely. Simply invite your team members to your workspace, and they will be able to see all meetings in the shared workspace and collaboratively edit meeting records.\n\n### What is a Meeting Workspace in SeaMeet AI Note Taker?\n\nA workspace is where you manage all your meetings, team members, and plans.\n\n#### How do I manage meetings in the workspace?\n\nAny transcribed meeting records will be stored in the workspace. You can manage future, ongoing, and completed meetings in the workspace.\n\n#### How do I collaborate with my team in the workspace?\n\nYou can invite team members to join the workspace to collaboratively view and edit meeting records. You can also set different permissions for better management of the workspace.\n\n#### How to Choose the Right Meeting AI Note Taker Subscription Plan for Your Team\n\nIf you want more transcription hours or advanced features, feel free to **upgrade your workspace plan** or **contact our customer service at seameet@seasalt.ai**. We will be happy to assist you.\n\n### How to Log In to SeaMeet AI Meeting Note Taker\n\nYou can log in to SeaMeet using your Google account or register using your email.\n\n### How to Edit AI-Generated Meeting Transcripts in SeaMeet\n\nYou can use the export to Google Docs feature to edit. Editing is currently not allowed on the SeaMeet meeting page, but this feature is expected to be supported soon.\n\n### Can I Download Meeting Audio Files with SeaMeet AI Note Taker?\n\nYes, after the meeting is finished, you can log back to SeaMeet to download the audio from the play bar.\n\n### Does SeaMeet AI Note Taker Support In-Person Meetings and Speaker Identification?\n\nYou can use a computer to open Google Meet for meeting recording during in-person meetings with SeaMeet AI Note Taker. However, features like changing the speaker for in-person meetings are not yet available and are expected to be provided in Q1 SeaMeet\'s Speaker ID feature helps identify different speakers in recorded meetings, but manual speaker assignment for in-person meetings is coming soon.\n\n### How to Manage Multiple Workspaces and Language Settings in SeaMeet AI Note Taker?\n\nIf you have multiple workspaces in SeaMeet AI Note Taker, you can store meetings in different workspaces separately. When scheduling meetings in Google Calendar, the storage location and language will be determined according to your default language and default workspace settings in "Personal Settings - Meeting Settings". If you use the Chrome application to invite SeaMeet, you can specify which workspace to store the meeting in, allowing for better organization of your AI meeting transcriptions.\n\n### How to Completely Disable Auto-Join Feature for SeaMeet AI Meeting Assistant?\n\nIf you\'ve turned off the auto-join feature but SeaMeet Copilot still joins your meetings, it\'s likely because the meeting was scheduled before you disabled the feature. To completely stop SeaMeet Copilot from automatically joining meetings:\n\nFirst, disconnect your Google Calendar to stop SeaMeet Copilot from synchronizing with your Google Calendar. Go to **Account** -> **Integration** to disconnect Google Calendar.\n\nIf SeaMeet Copilot still joins meetings after disconnecting, manually remove any pre-scheduled meetings from your meeting list. Go to **Meeting List** and find future meetings with the turquoise background. Simply click on the trash can icon to delete these meetings.\n\nThis ensures that your SeaMeet AI Meeting Assistant will no longer automatically join meetings without your explicit invitation.\n\n### How to Re-invite SeaMeet Copilot to a Meeting After Disconnection?\n\nAs a registered user of SeaMeet AI Note Taker, you can easily re-invite the copilot back to a meeting if the SeaMeet Copilot leaves or gets disconnected. To re-invite the copilot:\n\nGo to your meeting list in the SeaMeet dashboard\nClick on **Start Recording** for the specific meeting\nThe SeaMeet Copilot will rejoin the meeting to continue AI meeting transcription\n\nThis feature ensures you never miss important meeting content due to temporary disconnections.\n\n### Can Registered SeaMeet Users Access Meeting Records from Unregistered Participants?\n\nWhen using SeaMeet AI Note Taker, if you\'re an unregistered participant in a meeting, registered SeaMeet users can still access the meeting records under certain conditions:\n\n**Copilot Invitation**: If a registered user has invited the SeaMeet Copilot to the meeting, then that registered user will be able to see the meeting records in their SeaMeet dashboard.\n\n**Auto-Share Feature**: If the registered user has scheduled the meeting in their meeting list, they can use the auto-share feature to automatically share meeting records with all invited participants. To set this up, go to **General** -> **Auto Share** and choose **All participants in calendar event**.\n\nThis feature ensures seamless collaboration between registered and unregistered users in your AI meeting transcription workflow. For more detailed instructions, check out our [sharing tutorial](https://wiki.seasalt.ai/en/seameet/sharing/).\n\n### How to Access Meeting Transcriptions for Meetings Scheduled by Other Users in SeaMeet AI Note Taker?\n\nWhen using SeaMeet AI Meeting Assistant, registered users can receive meeting transcriptions for meetings scheduled by other users under specific conditions:\n\n**Direct Copilot Invitation**: If you\'re a registered user and you invite the SeaMeet Copilot to a meeting scheduled by another user, you will receive the meeting transcription in your SeaMeet dashboard.\n\n**Auto-Share Feature**: If the meeting owner has enabled the auto-share feature, the meeting transcription will be automatically shared with all invited participants, regardless of who scheduled the meeting.\n\nIf you haven\'t invited the copilot to the meeting and the meeting owner hasn\'t enabled auto-sharing, you won\'t receive the meeting transcription. This access control ensures that only authorized participants can view sensitive meeting content in your AI meeting transcription system.\n\n### How to View and Manage Auto-Sharing Email Settings in SeaMeet AI Note Taker?\n\nTo view and manage the email addresses set up for auto-sharing meeting records in SeaMeet AI Meeting Assistant:\n\nNavigate to your SeaMeet dashboard\nGo to **Workspace** -> **General** -> **Auto Share**\nIn the **Auto Share** section, you can see all email addresses configured for automatic meeting record sharing\n\nThis feature allows you to easily verify which email addresses will receive your AI-transcribed meeting records automatically, ensuring seamless collaboration with your team members.\n\n### Do I Need to Confirm Invitation Email for SeaMeet Copilot to Join Meeting?\n\nWhen using SeaMeet AI Meeting Assistant, you don\'t need to confirm the invitation email for the copilot to join your meeting. As long as you\'ve properly invited the SeaMeet Copilot to the meeting and have sufficient base minutes available in your account, the copilot will automatically join the meeting when it starts.\n\nThis seamless process ensures that your AI meeting transcription begins immediately without requiring manual confirmation, making it easy to capture all meeting content from the start.\n\n### What Are the Different Ways to Invite SeaMeet Copilot to a Meeting?\n\nYou don\'t have to rely solely on Google Calendar to invite the SeaMeet Copilot to your meetings. SeaMeet AI Meeting Assistant provides multiple flexible invitation methods to suit your workflow:\n\n**Google Calendar Invitation**: Simply invite `meet@seasalt.ai` to your Google Calendar event, and the copilot will automatically join your Google Meet session.\n\n**SeaMeet Extension**: Install the browser extension from the Chrome Web Store (also available on Edge). Once installed, open Google Meet and click "Start Recording" to invite the copilot directly through the extension.\n\n**Workspace Invitation**: Within your SeaMeet dashboard, click the "Start Recording" button, enter the Google Meet meeting code, and submit to add the meeting to your list.\n\nEach method offers seamless AI meeting transcription, allowing you to choose the approach that best fits your scheduling preferences. For detailed instructions on each method, check out our comprehensive [SeaMeet introduction tutorial](https://wiki.seasalt.ai/en/seameet/seameet-manual/01-seameet-intro/).\n\n### Can SeaMeet AI Note Taker Handle Multiple Meetings Simultaneously?\n\nNo, only users with team plans can host multiple meetings at the same time. If you are using an individual plan, you can only host one meeting at a time. The number of available copilots depends on the number of paid licenses. That is, if there are two paid licenses, you can invite two copilots to join the meetings.\n\nWith SeaMeet AI Meeting Assistant, individual plan users are limited to one concurrent meeting, while team plan subscribers can host multiple simultaneous meetings. The exact number of concurrent meetings depends on your paid license count. For example, with two paid licenses, you can have two copilots joining separate meetings simultaneously.\n\n### How Long Are Meeting Records Stored in SeaMeet AI Note Taker?\n\nCurrently, meetings do not have an expiration date. You can see the meeting duration of each meeting in the meeting list.\n\nWith SeaMeet AI Meeting Assistant, your meeting records are stored indefinitely in your workspace. You can access any past meeting transcription, summary, action items, and discussion topics at any time. To identify the duration of specific meetings, simply check the meeting list where each entry displays its total recording time. This permanent storage ensures you never lose important meeting information and can always refer back to previous discussions.\n\n### What Are the Pricing Details for Exceeding Base Minutes in SeaMeet AI Note Taker?\n\nAfter you exceed the 50 hours of base minutes, you will be charged $1 per hour. You can always check the remaining base minutes and the minutes used at the bottom of your sidebar.\n\nWith SeaMeet AI Meeting Assistant, users receive 50 base minutes per month with their subscription. If your team requires additional transcription time, you\'ll only pay $1 for each extra hour used. To monitor your usage, simply check the minutes counter located at the bottom of your SeaMeet sidebar, which displays both your remaining balance and total minutes consumed. This transparent pricing model ensures you only pay for what you use while having full visibility into your consumption.\n\n### What Happens When SeaMeet AI Note Taker Reaches Usage Limits?\n\nCurrently, there are only two situations that will cause the copilot to quit the recording. One is when a user with the free plan uses more than six hours in total, and the other is when a single meeting exceeds the limits of certain hours. For free plan users, the limit is one hour. For paid plan individual users, the limit is three hours, and for paid plan team users, the limit is five hours.\n\nWith SeaMeet AI Meeting Assistant, your recording session may end early if you reach specific usage thresholds. Free plan users have a total limit of 6 hours per month, with individual meetings capped at 1 hour. Paid individual plan subscribers can record meetings up to 3 hours long, while team plan users enjoy 5-hour meeting limits. These safeguards ensure fair usage across all plan types while providing adequate recording time for most business meetings.\n\n### How to Handle Multilingual Meetings with SeaMeet AI Note Taker?\n\nAlthough one can set the meeting language to **Detect Language**, we recommand users to set the meeting language to the primary language used in the meeting for optimal performance. One way to do deal with multiple languages is to set the meeting language to the primary language used in the meeting and switch to the other language mid-meeting when the conversation will be conducted in that language. The transcription will then have both the primary language and the other language.\n\nSeaMeet AI Meeting Assistant offers flexible solutions for multilingual meetings. For meetings conducted in multiple languages like English and Chinese, we recommend setting the primary language as your default. During the meeting, you can seamlessly switch languages using the language selector when the conversation shifts to the secondary language. This approach ensures accurate transcription in both languages while maintaining optimal performance. Our advanced AI can detect and transcribe multiple languages within the same meeting session.\n\n### Does SeaMeet AI Note Taker Support Video Recording of Meetings?\n\nNot yet, SeaMeet currently only supports transcribing and recording the audio of the meeting. Video recording is not supported at the moment.\n\nSeaMeet AI Meeting Assistant focuses exclusively on audio transcription and meeting note-taking capabilities. While we don\'t currently offer video recording functionality, our advanced AI captures comprehensive audio data to create detailed meeting transcripts, summaries, action items, and discussion topics. This audio-first approach ensures optimal performance and accuracy for your meeting documentation needs without the storage and processing overhead of video files.\n\n### How to Download Meeting Recordings with SeaMeet AI Note Taker?\n\nYes, user with paid plans can download the meeting recording. Free plan user can only listen to the recording on the SeaMeet platform.\n\nWith SeaMeet AI Meeting Assistant, downloading meeting recordings is available exclusively for paid plan subscribers. Individual and Team plan users can download audio recordings directly from the meeting page, while Free plan users can only stream their recordings through the SeaMeet platform. This premium feature allows you to keep local copies of your important meetings for offline access and archival purposes.\n\n### How to Re-invite SeaMeet AI Copilot to a Meeting on Mobile Devices After Disconnection?\n\nYou can invite the SeaMeet copilot to join the meeting again using a mobile device in the following two scenarios:\n\n**For meetings that have not yet had the copilot record**: You can invite `meet@seasalt.ai` to the meeting through Google Calendar, ensuring that the copilot joins the meeting on time to start recording.\n\n**For meetings where the copilot has already been invited**: Simply log in to SeaMeet on your mobile device -> go to the meeting list page -> click on "Start Meeting" -> and paste the Google Meet ID to invite the copilot to rejoin the meeting.\n\n> **Note**\n>\n> To invite SeaMeet to record the same meeting again, make sure that the "previous SeaMeet meeting record" has ended. If the meeting was previously being recorded by SeaMeet, it may take about 30 seconds to a minute to process after stopping the meeting.\n>\n> Be sure to wait until the previous recording has completely ended before making the second invitation, as otherwise, the system might determine that "the meeting is already being recorded," resulting in an invitation failure.\n\n### How to Use Team Workspace Hours for Auto-Join Meetings in SeaMeet AI Note Taker?\n\nCurrently, SeaMeet determines which plan\'s hours are deducted, **based on the workspace where the meeting is stored**.\nSo, if you want the feature of "automatically joined meetings" to use the team plan\'s hours and store the meeting records in the team workspace, you can set the default workspace to the team workspace by following this path: **Account** -> **Meeting Preference** -> **Default Settings** -> **Default Workspace**.\n\n### What Are the Key Differences Between SeaMeet Individual and Team Plans for AI Meeting Note Taker?\n\nHere are the main differences between the two plans:\n\nThe team plan allows multiple people to collaborate in the workspace, where everyone can view transcriptions in the backend, download audio, and export using Google Docs, etc.\nThe team plan supports multiple simultaneous meetings, whereas the individual plan allows only one copilot to join a meeting at a time. For individual plan users, if the copilot is still attending Meeting A and the user starts another Meeting B, the copilot will not be able to join Meeting B.\n\n### Why Was My SeaMeet AI Meeting Recording Incomplete and How to Fix It?\n\nThere are various reasons why a meeting might not be fully recorded. Please first check if the bot was admitted into the meeting by the host and successfully joined the meeting room. If so, confirm whether the bot stayed throughout the entire meeting or was removed by a participant at some point.\n\nIf the bot remained in the meeting room the entire time, please verify whether the recording and transcript are complete. Then send the SeaMeet meeting record link along with your issue description to <email: seameet@seasalt.ai> for further assistance.\n\n### How to Fix SeaMeet AI Bot Join Issues and Spinning Loading Indicator?\n\nPlease ask the Google Meet meeting host to check whether the bot\'s join request was received.\nIf not, go to the SeaMeet meeting list to confirm whether the meeting was successfully created.\n\n### How to Resolve SeaMeet AI Meeting Audio File "File Not Found" Error?\n\nIt may still be processing within five minutes after the meeting ends. If the file is still missing after ten minutes, please send the SeaMeet meeting record link to <email: seameet@seasalt.ai> for further investigation.\n\n### Why Can\'t I Download SeaMeet AI Meeting Audio Files and How to Fix It?\n\nAudio downloads are currently only available for "Personal" and "Team" plan users. Free plan users do not have access to downloads yet.\n\n### How to Record Bilingual Meetings in Chinese and English with SeaMeet AI Note Taker?\n\nTo conduct a bilingual meeting, we recommend selecting "Traditional Chinese" as the transcription language. It can simultaneously recognize English speech.\n\n### How is SeaMeet AI Meeting Assistant Usage Time Calculated for Transcription?\n\nSeaMeet AI Meeting Assistant only starts counting recording time after the bot successfully joins the Google Meet room. If the bot does not enter the meeting, no time is counted toward your transcription quota.\nWhen you bind your Google Calendar, the bot can automatically attempt to join meetings, but time is only recorded when the bot is admitted and actively records content.\n\nFor paid plans, the usage time resets every month, allowing you to use your full monthly quota for AI meeting transcription. This ensures you get the most value from your SeaMeet AI Note Taker subscription.\n\n### Can Someone Other Than the Meeting Host Invite the SeaMeet AI Bot for Transcription?\n\nYes, anyone can invite the SeaMeet AI Meeting Assistant bot, but the meeting host must approve the bot\'s entry for transcription to begin.\nThe meeting recording will be associated with the account that invited the bot, and time usage will be calculated accordingly.\n\nIf the meeting host is not a SeaMeet user, they cannot invite the bot on your behalf unless they also have a SeaMeet account. This security measure ensures that only authorized participants can initiate AI meeting transcription.\n\n### What Happens After Exceeding the Monthly Usage Limit for SeaMeet AI Note Taker?\n\nEach SeaMeet AI Meeting Assistant plan includes a monthly transcription quota. Once you exceed your plan\'s quota, additional usage will incur extra charges at the standard rate, but your AI meeting transcription service will continue without interruption.\n\nThis pay-as-you-go model ensures that your important meetings are never missed due to reaching your usage limit, while providing transparent pricing for any additional transcription time needed.\n\n### Where Do "View Full Meeting Record" Links in SeaMeet Summary Emails Lead After Meeting Ends?\n\nAfter a meeting ends, the "View full meeting record" link in SeaMeet AI Meeting Assistant summary emails has been redesigned to provide a better experience for recipients.\n\nWorkspace users who click the link will be taken to the "SeaMeet meeting page" where they can access full meeting details.\n\nNon-workspace users will see the "SeaMeet public share page," which is view-only and cannot be edited.\n\nIf the recipient hasn\'t been invited or granted access, the content will be masked for security, ensuring your meeting information remains protected.\n\n### How to Manage Permissions for Shared Meeting Pages in SeaMeet AI Note Taker?\n\nEach meeting in SeaMeet AI Meeting Assistant has its own "Share List" where you can manage permissions for shared meeting pages.\n\nTo edit the share list or review access requests, click the Share button in the top-right corner of the meeting page.\n\nIf sharing is set to "Invite calendar attendees," they will be automatically added to the view list, making it easy to collaborate with all meeting participants on your AI-transcribed meeting notes.\n\n### How to Subscribe to Annual AI Meeting Transcription Plans for SeaMeet Note Taker?\n\nThe annual subscription plan for SeaMeet AI Meeting Note Taker is currently under development and will be available soon to provide cost-effective AI-powered meeting transcription services.\n\nIf you need an annual AI meeting transcription subscription now, please contact our sales team at <email: seameet@seasalt.ai> and we\'ll set up your annual SeaMeet AI Note Taker plan manually.\n\nAnnual plans offer significant cost savings and convenience by pre-paying for your SeaMeet AI Meeting Transcription and Note Taking services for an entire year, ensuring uninterrupted access to automated meeting summaries, action items extraction, and real-time transcription features.\n\n### Why Does My SeaMeet AI Meeting Transcription Subscription Only Last Until Month End?\n\nSeaMeet Personal Plan for AI meeting transcription and note-taking is billed monthly at $9.99, with billing cycles running from the 1st to the end of each month.\nIf you subscribe to SeaMeet AI Note Taker mid-month, a prorated charge will apply based on remaining days (e.g., subscribe on 4/20, you pay 1/3 of $9.99 for the remaining days of AI meeting transcription services).\n\n### Does Adding Team Members to SeaMeet AI Meeting Note Taker Increase Subscription Costs?\n\nYes. In the SeaMeet AI Meeting Transcription Team Plan, each additional team member seat incurs a charge for accessing AI-powered meeting notes and transcription features, which will be billed at the start of the next month.\n\n### Can SeaMeet AI Transcription Improve Recognition of Company-Specific Terms and Jargon?\n\nYes! SeaMeet AI Meeting Note Taker can improve transcription accuracy for your company-specific terminology. Please provide a glossary of commonly misrecognized industry terms, product names, or company jargon so we can help enhance the AI transcription accuracy for your meetings.\n\n### Does SeaMeet AI Meeting Note Taker Support Microsoft Teams Integration?\n\nYes. Microsoft Teams integration for SeaMeet AI meeting transcription is currently generally available. You\'ll be able to paste the Teams meeting link to invite the SeaMeet AI transcription bot for automated meeting notes and summaries.\n\n### How to Change Login Password for SeaMeet AI Meeting Transcription Account?\n\nSeaMeet AI Note Taker primarily uses Google login or OTP-based authentication for secure access to meeting transcription services. Traditional password login is reserved for enterprise AI meeting assistant clients and currently cannot be edited directly by individual users.\n\n### How to Delete SeaMeet AI Meeting Note Taker Account or Workspace?\n\nSeaMeet AI Meeting Transcription service does not yet offer self-serve account or workspace deletion.\nTo prevent the AI meeting bot from auto-joining future meetings, you can disconnect your Google Calendar from SeaMeet.\nIf you need to delete an AI meeting transcription workspace, please email <email: seameet@seasalt.ai>.\n⚠️ Note: Deleted SeaMeet AI note-taking workspaces and meeting transcripts cannot be recovered.\n\n### Is SeaMeet AI Meeting Transcription Secure?\n\nYes — data security is our top priority when recording and transcribing meetings with AI technology.\nSee our [Terms of Service](https://seasalt.ai/terms/) for details on our AI meeting transcription usage terms and security practices.\nFor information on what meeting data we collect and how we use it for AI note-taking, see our [Privacy Policy](https://seasalt.ai/privacy/).\nWe use WAF protection via Azure and AWS to prevent malicious access to meeting transcripts, and FIPS-compliant encryption to protect sensitive meeting data.\nSeaMeet AI Meeting Note Taker complies with CASA Level 2 security standards, performs regular Nessus vulnerability scans, and meets HECVAT standards with US data residency guarantees for meeting transcriptions.\n\n### Can SeaMeet AI Meeting Bot Auto-Join Without Host Permission?\n\nNo — due to privacy and security concerns (especially for external meetings), host approval is required before the SeaMeet AI transcription bot can join and start recording meeting notes.\n\nIf you\'re unsure why the AI meeting assistant bot failed to join your meeting, please check this troubleshooting guide.\n\n### Can I Customize the SeaMeet AI Meeting Bot Display Name?\n\nCurrently, there are no plans to support customizing the SeaMeet AI transcription bot\'s display name or nickname in meeting rooms.\n\n### Can I Mute the SeaMeet AI Meeting Transcription Bot During Recordings?\n\nDue to security policy constraints, muting the SeaMeet AI meeting note-taking bot during live transcription sessions is not currently supported.\n\n### How to Disable SeaMeet AI Meeting Assistant Popup in Google Meet?\n\nThe SeaMeet AI meeting transcription popup is a feature of the Chrome browser extension for automated note-taking.\nTo disable the AI meeting assistant popup, click the extension icon in the upper-right corner of Chrome and choose Manage Extensions to adjust the SeaMeet AI transcription settings.\n\n\n### What is a Meeting Workspace in SeaMeet AI Note Taker?\n\nA workspace is where you manage all meetings, team members, and plans. You can create a shared workspace for your company, department, or team, allowing invited users to jointly manage all meeting records stored in this workspace.\n\n### How to Manage Meetings in Your SeaMeet AI Note Taker Workspace\n\nMeeting records will be stored in the designated workspace. You can manage future, ongoing, or completed meetings in the workspace.\n\n### How to Collaborate with Your Team in SeaMeet AI Meeting Workspace\n\nYou can invite team members to join the workspace on the "Workspace Settings - Users" page to collaboratively view and edit meeting records. You can also set different permissions to better manage the workspace.\n\nOnce you send the invitation, the invited users can register and log in using the link in the invitation email and join the invited workspace.\n\nUser permissions are divided into "Admin" and "Member".\n- Admin\n    - Can view all meetings in the workspace.\n    - Can delete meetings.\n    - Can invite users to the workspace and grant any permissions.\n    - Can remove users.\n- Member\n    - Default can view all meetings in the workspace but can be adjusted to view personal meetings only.\n    - Cannot delete meetings.\n    - Can invite users to the workspace but can only invite as "Member".\n    - Cannot remove users.\n\n### How to Choose the Best AI Meeting Transcription Plan for Your Team\'s Note-Taking Needs\n\nIf you need more AI meeting transcription hours, advanced automated summary features, or enhanced team collaboration tools, feel free to upgrade your SeaMeet workspace plan or contact our customer service <email: seameet@seasalt.ai>. We will be happy to help you select the optimal AI meeting note-taking solution for your organization.\n\n### How to Create a New Meeting Workspace in SeaMeet AI Note Taker\n\nIf you want to create multiple workspaces for different units, click the "Workspace List" at the top right of the screen. Then click "Create" in the "Workspace List" to start creating a new workspace.\n\n### How to Delete AI Meeting Transcripts and Notes in SeaMeet?\n\nCurrently, only users with "Admin" permissions can delete AI-generated meeting transcripts and notes. Click the "..." next to the meeting title to delete the AI meeting record. Click "Delete" to confirm the deletion of the meeting transcription and automated summary.\n\n### How to Set Default AI Transcription Language and Workspace for Meeting Notes?\n\nClick "Personal Settings - Meeting Settings" to configure your personal default AI transcription language and default workspace for meeting notes.\nDefault AI Transcription Language: This is the default language used for AI meeting transcription when you schedule "future meetings" in Google Calendar. You can still adjust the meeting recording language for individual AI note-taking sessions.\nDefault Meeting Workspace: This is the default workspace where AI-generated meeting transcripts and summaries from "future meetings" scheduled in Google Calendar will be stored.\n\n### How to Change SeaMeet AI Meeting Assistant Interface Language?\n\nTo adjust the SeaMeet AI meeting transcription interface display language, go to "Personal Settings - Appearance" and change the interface language for your AI note-taking dashboard.\n\n\n### What is a Workspace Owner in SeaMeet AI Note Taker?\n\nThe user account that creates the workspace will be considered Workspace Owner, and the subscribed plan will apply to all workspaces under their administration. \n\nIf your team has multiple workspaces and you wish to use one subscription for all of them, please ensure that the workspace owner creates all the workspaces. For example, if the workspace owner creates two workspaces and subscribes to a team plan, then the team plan will apply to both workspaces.\n\n### How Does SeaMeet Count Team Members in AI Meeting Transcription Plans?\n\nThe workspace owner manages all users across SeaMeet AI meeting note-taking workspace(s). The total number of unique accounts, excluding duplicates, determines the total user count for AI transcription billing.\n\nFor example, if the workspace owner invites colleagues A, B, C, and D to two AI meeting transcription workspaces, even if user B can access both workspaces for meeting notes, the subscription plan will only count 5 users (including the workspace owner), not 6 users.\n\n\n### How to Invite the SeaMeet Copilot for AI Meeting Transcription?\n\nSeaMeet supports multiple invitation methods, and you can choose one of the following three methods to invite the copilot:\n\nWorkspace Invitation:\n   - Click the "Start Recording" button.\n   - Enter the Google Meet meeting code and submit.\n   - The meeting will automatically be added to the meeting list.\n\nSeaMeet Extension Invitation:\n   - Install the extension from the Chrome Web Store (also available on Edge).\n   - After installation, open Google Meet, and the extension will automatically open.\n   - Click "Start Recording" to invite the copilot to the meeting.\n   - Allow the copilot to join and start recording the meeting.\n\nGoogle Calendar Invitation:\n   - Invite the SeaMeet copilot <email: meet@seasalt.ai> to the meeting in Google Calendar.\n   - The SeaMeet copilot will join the Google Meet meeting on time.\n\n### How to Switch the Default Transcription Language in SeaMeet AI Note Taker?\n\nGo to the "Account" -> "Preference" page.\nSet the default meeting recording language for your account for future invitations to the copilot. \nWhen starting a "Scheduled Meeting" recording, you will see that the default recording language has changed.\n\n### How do I switch the language for an individual meeting?\n\nEnter the individual meeting page and click "Current Meeting Language".\nChoose another expected meeting recording language from the menu.\nAfter selecting, the recording will proceed with the new model.\n\n### How do I switch the meeting recording language on the SeaMeet widget?\n\nStart recording a meeting with the SeaMeet Copilot.\nChange the recording language by clicking on the dropdown menu.\nChoose the language you need.\n\n### Can I switch the meeting language during a meeting?\n\nYes, you can switch the meeting record language at any time before or during the meeting.\n\n\n### How to Set Up Auto-Sharing of Meeting Records in SeaMeet AI Note Taker?\n\nYou can adjust the recipients of automatically shared meeting records in the "General" section of the "Workspace".\n\n### What Auto-Sharing Options Are Available for AI Meeting Transcripts in SeaMeet?\n\nSeaMeet AI Meeting Note Taker offers the following automated sharing options for meeting transcripts and summaries:\n"Only share with me" - When you invite the AI copilot to transcribe a meeting, the system will automatically send the AI-generated meeting notes and summary to your inbox once the meeting ends.\n"All participants in calendar event" - When the AI meeting transcription is complete, the system will automatically send the meeting notes and AI summary to all attendees invited via Google Calendar.\n"Share with attendees who have the same domain as me" - When the AI meeting transcription ends, the system will automatically send meeting notes to all attendees who have the same email domain as you. For example, if you\'re using "@seasalt.ai", in a meeting with attendees using "@seasalt.ai" and "@client-company.com", the AI meeting notes will only be sent to attendees with the "@seasalt.ai" domain for security. It only applies to those with private email addresses sharing your domain, not to those using public email domains like Gmail, Hotmail, and Outlook.\n"Off for anyone including myself" - No AI meeting transcripts or summaries will be sent after the meeting ends.\n\n### What is the Additional List Feature for AI Meeting Transcript Auto-Sharing?\n\nThe additional list feature allows you to send AI-generated meeting transcripts and summaries to recipients who did not attend the meeting. You can send CC and BCC of the AI meeting notes to additional recipients. The CC and BCC recipients can also be an email group for broader distribution of meeting transcriptions.\n\nOne very useful feature of the additional list is the blocklist for AI meeting notes. When you choose the option to send the AI meeting transcript to all attendees in the calendar event, you can exclude certain attendees from receiving the meeting transcription by adding them to the blocklist.\n\n### Do I Need to Enable Additional List Feature for AI Meeting Transcript Sharing?\n\nYes, you need to enable the additional list feature first before you can use it to share AI meeting transcripts and summaries with additional recipients.\n\n\n### How to Enable Auto-Join for AI Meeting Transcription in SeaMeet Note Taker?\n\nGo to the SeaMeet AI transcription settings page, click "Integration", and connect SeaMeet to the Google account you want for automated meeting note-taking.\nGo to the "Meeting Preference" page, click "Auto-join Meetings", enable auto join meetings for AI transcription, and select "All Meetings in My Calendar".\n\n### What Google Calendar Settings Are Required for SeaMeet AI Auto-Join Transcription?\n\nWhen scheduling a new meeting in Google Calendar for AI transcription, make sure to click add a video meeting, so that there is a video meeting link, and SeaMeet AI Note Taker can correctly add the meeting to the transcription list. Meetings without video meeting links will not be automatically joined by the SeaMeet AI meeting bot.\n\n### How to View Scheduled Meetings for AI Auto-Join Transcription in SeaMeet?\n\nAfter enabling the auto-join meetings feature for AI transcription, you can find the added meetings in the meetings list. When the meeting starts, SeaMeet AI Note Taker will automatically join and start recording meeting transcripts and generating summaries.\n\n### How to Disable Auto-Join Feature for AI Meeting Transcription in SeaMeet?\n\nFirst, please disconnect your Google Calendar in order to stop SeaMeet AI Copilot from synchronizing with your Google Calendar for automated transcription. Go to "Account" -> "Integration" to disconnect Google Calendar.\n\nAfter disconnecting, if SeaMeet AI Copilot still joins meetings automatically for transcription, it is because the meeting was scheduled before the disconnection. In this case, you can manually remove the meeting from your AI transcription list. Go to Meeting List and find the future meetings with the turquoise background. Simply click on the trash can icon to delete the meeting from AI note-taking schedule.\n\n\n### What are AI Summary Templates in SeaMeet Meeting Note Taker?\n\nAn AI summary template is a customizable format for automated meeting summaries that allows users to generate AI-powered meeting minutes tailored to the specific nature of their meetings. Each SeaMeet workspace will have its own list of AI summary templates for different meeting types.\n\n### What Built-in AI Summary Templates Are Available in SeaMeet Meeting Transcription?\n\nSeaMeet AI Meeting Note Taker provides a comprehensive set of built-in AI summary templates covering common business meetings and industry-specific transcription needs:\n- [Default] SeaMeet standard summary\n- [Custom] Weekly Department Meeting\n- [Custom] Podcast Recording\n- [Custom] Lecture Notes\n- [Custom] All-Hands Meeting\n- [Custom] Client Meeting\n- [Custom] Legal Case Preparation\n- [Custom] Job Interview Record\n- [Custom] Sales Meeting\n- [Custom] Daily Stand-up Meeting\n- [Custom] Academic Affairs Meeting\n- [Custom] Project Management Meeting\n- [Custom] One-on-One Meeting\n- [Custom] Journalist Interview Records\n- [Custom] Requirement Discussion Meeting\n- [Custom] Product Development Meeting\n- [Custom] Medical Appointment Records\n- [Custom] Strategy Planning Meeting\n\n### How to Apply AI Summary Templates to Meeting Transcriptions in SeaMeet?\n\nAfter the AI meeting transcription is complete, click the "Summary Template" icon next to the AI-generated meeting summary.\nIn the drop-down menu of the pop-up window, select the AI summary template you want to apply to your meeting notes.\nSelect Save to regenerate the AI meeting summary with the chosen template format.\n\n### Can I Apply AI Templates to Recurring Meeting Transcriptions?\n\nYes, if you have a fixed routine meeting and want to apply a specific AI summary template for consistent meeting notes, you can apply a template to a series of meetings. After application, the AI template will be automatically applied whenever a new meeting transcription of this series is created.\n\n### How to Set Default AI Summary Template for New Meeting Transcriptions?\n\nWhen recording a new meeting with SeaMeet AI Note Taker, the default AI template will be applied as the main summary setting for automated transcription. You can go to the AI summary template list to set other summary templates as default options for meeting notes.\n\n### How to Create Custom AI Summary Templates for Meeting Transcription?\n\nYou can click "Add Template" to create a new AI summary template for meeting notes.\nFill in the name of the AI template for your specific meeting type.\nFill in the prompt words to describe the format and precautions for the AI-generated meeting minutes.\nAfter completing the template setup, click Save to add it to the AI summary template list.\n\n### How to Edit or Delete AI Summary Templates in SeaMeet Meeting Note Taker?\n\nIf you want to edit or delete an existing AI summary template for meeting transcription, click (⋮) on the right side of the individual template and select the action you want to perform.\n\n### Who Can Use Custom AI Summary Templates in SeaMeet Meeting Transcription?\n\nThe custom AI summary template function is only available for Individual and Team plans of SeaMeet AI Note Taker. Users must have Owner or Admin permissions for the workspace to create and manage AI meeting summary templates.\n\n\n### How to Use AI Speaker Identification for In-Person Meeting Transcription?\n\nWhen recording in-person meetings using Google Meet with SeaMeet AI Note Taker, you can use the "AI Speaker ID" feature to resplit the transcript and specify how many speakers to distinguish:\nBased on the actual number of meeting participants, you can use "AI Speaker Identification" to resplit the meeting transcript and specify how many speakers the AI should distinguish.\nDuring the AI speaker identification process, you can leave the meeting at any time and return to view the results when the AI transcription analysis is complete.\nWhen AI identification is complete, you can see participants distinguished as different speakers in the meeting notes (e.g., Speaker 1, Speaker 2, Speaker 3).\n\n### How to Edit Speaker Labels in AI Meeting Transcripts with SeaMeet?\n\nAfter completing AI speaker identification, you can listen to individual speakers in the meeting transcript to confirm and change to the correct speaker labels:\nListen to individual speaker recordings in the AI meeting transcript and confirm the actual speakers.\nChoose an existing participant or create a new one to replace the original AI-identified speaker.\nChoose whether the "new speaker" should replace a single dialogue or all dialogue segments of the "old speaker" in the AI transcript.\nOnce all speakers in the AI meeting transcript have been replaced with the correct speaker labels, the transcript adjustment is complete.\n\n### How to Regenerate AI Meeting Summary After Editing Speaker Labels?\n\nAfter replacing all speakers in the AI transcript, you can regenerate the meeting summary based on the adjusted transcript:\nAfter replacing all speakers in the AI meeting transcript, you can regenerate the AI meeting summary based on the corrected speaker labels.\nDuring the process of regenerating the AI meeting summary, you can leave the meeting at any time and return to view it when the AI processing is complete.\nAfter completing the AI summary regeneration, you can view the updated AI-generated summary based on the corrected speaker identifications.\n\n\n### How to Access AI Meeting Transcripts and Notes in SeaMeet?\n\nWhen you invite the SeaMeet AI Copilot to join a meeting, it will create a meeting entry in your workspace\'s AI transcription list. Click on the meeting title to access detailed AI-generated meeting information, including real-time meeting transcription, AI-identified discussion topics, automated summary, and extracted action items.\n\n### How to Browse AI Meeting Transcripts in SeaMeet Meeting Note Taker?\n\nClick the "Meeting List" page to see the list of AI-transcribed, ongoing, and upcoming meetings. Then click the meeting title to view the AI-generated meeting records and automated summaries.\n\n### What Happens if I Haven\'t Allowed SeaMeet AI Bot to Join Google Meet?\n\nIf you have not yet allowed the SeaMeet AI transcription copilot to join the Google Meet room, you will see a notification message. You need to allow the AI meeting bot to enter the meeting room in Google Meet to start automated transcription and note-taking.\n\n### What Information is Included in AI Meeting Transcripts and Notes?\n\nAI meeting records include real-time meeting transcripts with AI speaker identification and speaking time tracking, as well as automatically extracted AI meeting summaries, action items, and discussion topics that are generated at regular intervals during the meeting by SeaMeet\'s AI technology.\n\n### Which Languages Does SeaMeet AI Transcription Support for Meeting Notes?\n\nSeaMeet\'s AI transcript recognition is specially trained for the Taiwanese market and can recognize mixed Chinese and English conversation scenarios for accurate multilingual meeting transcription and note-taking.\n\n\n### What AI Analytics Does SeaMeet Provide During Meeting Transcription?\n\nDuring the meeting, SeaMeet AI will automatically extract meeting summaries, action items, and discussion topics from the conversation at regular intervals, providing real-time AI-powered meeting insights and automated note-taking.\n\n### What is Included in SeaMeet\'s AI Meeting Summary?\n\nSeaMeet AI automatically generates comprehensive meeting summaries from the conversation during the meeting, using advanced natural language processing to extract key insights and decisions.\n\n### What are AI-Extracted Action Items in SeaMeet Meeting Transcription?\n\nSeaMeet AI automatically extracts and identifies action items from the conversation during the meeting, helping teams track follow-up tasks and responsibilities from meeting discussions.\n\n### What are AI-Identified Discussion Topics in SeaMeet Meeting Notes?\n\nSeaMeet AI automatically identifies and extracts key discussion topics from the conversation during the meeting, organizing meeting content into structured themes for better understanding and follow-up.\n\n### What are Collaborative Team Notes in SeaMeet AI Meeting Assistant?\n\nIn addition to AI-generated notes, the team can also write down other content they want to record in the collaboratively edited team notes, such as meeting agendas, resolutions, and additional context that complements the AI meeting transcription.\n\n### What Information is Included in Real-Time AI Meeting Transcripts?\n\nReal-time AI meeting transcripts include speaker identification and speaking time tracking. SeaMeet\'s AI transcript recognition is specially trained for the Taiwanese market and can accurately recognize mixed Chinese and English conversation scenarios for comprehensive meeting documentation.\n\n\n### How to Play Meeting Recordings with AI Transcript Synchronization in SeaMeet?\n\nClick the play bar at the bottom of the meeting page to replay the full recording of the meeting with synchronized AI transcription. You can choose to drag the recording bar, fast-forward 10 seconds, pause/play, rewind 10 seconds, and other functions. The currently playing segment will be highlighted in the AI-generated transcript for easy reference.\n\n### How to Play Individual Conversation Segments in AI Meeting Transcripts?\n\nWhen the mouse hovers over a segment of the AI transcript, a play button will appear. Click it to play the corresponding audio segment that matches the AI-generated transcript text for precise review.\n\n\n### How to End AI Meeting Transcription Recording in SeaMeet Note Taker?\n\nYou can end an AI meeting transcription recording in SeaMeet by either:\nPressing the end meeting recording button on the SeaMeet AI transcription page\nManually pressing the end meeting button on the SeaMeet browser extension\n\n### What Happens if I Forget to End AI Meeting Transcription Recording?\n\nIf you forget to manually end the AI meeting transcription recording, the SeaMeet AI copilot will leave the Google Meet room automatically under the following conditions:\n30 seconds after all participants have left the meeting room\nIf a user remains in the meeting room, the AI copilot will wait 15 minutes to confirm if the meeting is paused. If no one speaks within 15 minutes, the AI transcription bot will automatically leave and finalize the meeting notes.\n\n\n### How to Add Labels to AI Meeting Transcripts in SeaMeet?\n\nYou can add labels to AI meeting transcripts in SeaMeet by:\nGoing to the "Meeting List" page and clicking on the AI meeting transcript you want to add labels to\nClicking the "+" sign to manage the labels for that meeting transcription\nCreating new labels for the workspace directly in the meeting and adding them to the AI meeting notes by entering label text that has not been created in the workspace in the search box and clicking create new label\n\n### How to Manage Labels for AI Meeting Transcripts in SeaMeet?\n\nYou can manage labels for AI meeting transcripts in SeaMeet by:\nGoing to the "Workspace Settings" -> "Label Management" page, or linking to this page from the meeting label management page\nClicking the "New Label" button in the top right corner to add a label to the AI transcription workspace\nClicking the "..." to the right of each label to edit or delete the label for organizing meeting notes\n\n\n### Can I Upload External Audio Files for AI Transcription in SeaMeet Note Taker?\n\nYes, SeaMeet AI Copilot allows you to upload external audio files for AI-powered transcription. This feature is perfect for meetings recorded outside the platform or other audio recordings requiring automated transcription and AI-generated summaries.\n\n### What Audio File Formats Does SeaMeet AI Transcription Support?\n\nSeaMeet AI Meeting Note Taker supports multiple audio file formats for AI transcription, including: .aac, .flac, .m4a, .mp3, .mp4, .ogg, .opus, .wav, .webm, .wma, .wmv.\n\n### How to Upload Audio Files for AI Transcription in SeaMeet?\n\nTo upload audio files for AI transcription on SeaMeet:\nNavigate to the "File List" page and click the "Upload Audio File" button\nSelect the correct file format from the AI-supported formats\nAdjust AI transcription settings including:\n   - Language of the audio for AI processing\n   - Meeting title for the AI transcript\nOptionally set the meeting timestamp (or let the system assign the current date and time by default)\nClick the "Start" button to begin AI transcription and automated summary generation\n\n### What AI Features Are Available for Uploaded Audio Files in SeaMeet?\n\nSeaMeet AI treats uploaded audio files just like scheduled meetings, offering comprehensive AI-powered features:\n- Editing capabilities for fine-tuning the AI transcript and automated summary\n- AI-extracted action items and discussed topics tracking\n- Collaboration tools for sharing AI meeting notes with your team or integrating with Google Docs\n\n### What is AI Speaker ID Feature in SeaMeet Meeting Transcription?\n\nAI Speaker ID is an advanced feature that helps users optimize their meeting transcription experience by differentiating between multiple speakers in a meeting. It uses AI-powered audio diarization to automatically identify and label speakers in the meeting transcription.\n\n### How Does AI Speaker ID Work in SeaMeet Meeting Transcription?\n\nWhen a meeting has multiple speakers, AI Speaker ID works through advanced machine learning:\nProviding the number of speakers in the audio file for accurate AI diarization\nSeaMeet AI differentiates speakers using generic naming like "speaker 1" and "speaker 2"\nUsers can then label speakers with correct names by choosing "Change Speaker" after clicking on the AI-identified name\nUsers can change speaker names throughout the whole AI transcript or just for chosen lines\n\n### How Many Speakers Does AI Speaker ID Work Best With in Meeting Transcription?\n\nAI Speaker ID works best with 2-6 people for optimal meeting transcription accuracy. AI performance may degrade with larger groups due to voice overlap and complexity.\n\n### What Happens After AI Audio Transcription is Complete in SeaMeet?\n\nAfter AI transcription is complete:\nReturn to your "File List" to access the AI-generated transcript and automated summary\nThe AI transcript and summary will be automatically generated with speaker identification\nYou can then edit and refine the AI results as needed, including action items and discussion topics\n\n\n### Which Browsers Support SeaMeet AI Meeting Transcription Extension?\n\nSeaMeet AI Meeting Note Taker offers browser extension support for many different browsers, including Arc, Brave, Edge, and Chrome for seamless AI meeting transcription integration.\n\n### How to Install SeaMeet AI Meeting Transcription Browser Extension?\n\nSimply click the "Install SeaMeet Extension" button on the SeaMeet website to install the AI meeting transcription browser extension for automated note-taking in Google Meet.\n\n### Why Install the SeaMeet AI Meeting Transcription Browser Extension?\n\nInstalling the SeaMeet AI meeting transcription browser extension ensures you will always have AI-powered note-taking and automated meeting summaries on your side in Google Meet sessions.\n\n### How Does SeaMeet AI Extension Integrate with Google Workspace for Meeting Transcription?\n\nFor users that work with Google Workspace, you can leverage SeaMeet\'s seamless AI integration with Google Meet, Google Calendar, and Google Docs to further optimize your automated meeting documentation and AI note-taking process.\n\n### How to Connect Google Calendar to SeaMeet for AI Meeting Transcription?\n\nYou can connect your Google Calendar to SeaMeet AI Note Taker, allowing the AI copilot to automatically join meetings or manually input the Google Meet code to start AI transcription and automated note-taking.\n\n\n### How to Export AI Meeting Transcripts to Google Docs?\n\nAfter the AI meeting transcription ends, the meeting record will be exported as a Google Docs document. Click the button in the top right corner of the page to open Google Docs, which contains all the AI-generated information from the just-concluded meeting, including transcripts, summaries, and action items.\n\n### How to Connect Google Drive to SeaMeet for AI Meeting Note Export?\n\nTo export AI meeting transcripts as a Google Docs document, please log in at https://meet.seasalt.ai and bind the SeaMeet AI workspace to a Google Drive for automated meeting note storage.\n\n### How to Automatically Export AI Meeting Transcripts to Google Docs?\n\nClick the Google Docs button in the top right corner of the AI meeting transcription page to access the corresponding AI-generated meeting record in Google Docs with automated summaries and action items.\n\n### How to Export Your SeaMeet Meeting Notes to Google Docs\n\n1.  First, connect your Google Drive account in the **Integration** settings of your SeaMeet account.\n2.  After a meeting, you can click the Google Docs button on the meeting page in your SeaMeet workspace to export the meeting record.\n3.  You can then find the meeting transcript and summary in a Google Doc in your Google Drive.';export{e as default};
